{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothTaylorBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothTaylorBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothRationalIndex","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.WronskianHeight"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_add_le_index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_add_le_index","kind":"theorem","line":512,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L512-L527","doc":"The real instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.seminorm_coeff_translate_add_le_index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.seminorm_coeff_translate_add_le_index","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L455-L510","doc":"**The Taylor tail with every budget folded in.**  Everything step 2 needs except the\narithmetic of the exponents: the index hypothesis at `α` restricts the sum, the degree bound\ncounts it, the height bound sizes each term, and `S` is whatever uniform bound the caller can\nprove on `∏_h G_h^{n_h−i_h}` over the surviving multi-indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_le","kind":"theorem","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L447-L453","doc":"The real instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.seminorm_coeff_translate_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.seminorm_coeff_translate_le","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L410-L445","doc":"**The height budget for a translate.**  `f (coeff n (translate α P)) ≤ #box · H · (2B)^{Σ r}`\n— the multivariate analogue of `WronskianHeight`'s budget, against any submultiplicative\nseminorm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.finsuppSum_eq_sum_univ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.finsuppSum_eq_sum_univ","kind":"theorem","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L406-L408","doc":"The total degree of a multi-index, as a sum over all coordinates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_add_le_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_add_le_prod","kind":"theorem","line":391,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L391-L398","doc":"The real instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.seminorm_coeff_translate_add_le_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.seminorm_coeff_translate_add_le_prod","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L369-L389","doc":"**The Taylor tail, bounded per coordinate.**  The form step 2 actually consumes: the index\nhypothesis at `α` restricts which `n` appear in the sum, and each surviving term carries\n`∏_h G_h^{n_h−i_h}` rather than a single power of a single `G`.\n\nStated against an arbitrary `SubmultSeminorm` rather than `|·|` on `ℝ`.  The `ℝ` instance is the\none step 2 uses over `ℤ`; the `ℂ` instance (`submultSeminorm_norm_complex`) is what the `𝓞 K` case\nneeds, because there the estimate has to run at a complex embedding.  Generalising was cheaper\nthan a second copy, and the `abs_` statements below are now one line each. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.sum_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.SubmultSeminorm.sum_le","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L358-L367","doc":"`f` of a finite sum is at most the sum of the `f`s.  The structure carries `add_le` only in\nbinary form; this is the iterated version every estimate here actually uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_translateMatrix_le_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_translateMatrix_le_prod","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L351-L356","doc":"**The real instance of the usable bound.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.seminorm_translateMatrix_le_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.seminorm_translateMatrix_le_prod","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L232-L349","doc":"**The usable bound: one `G_h` per coordinate.**  `f(binom(n,i)·γ^{n−i}) ≤ 2^{|n|}·∏_h\nG_h^{n_h−i_h}`.  Same peeling as `seminorm_translateMatrix_le_pow`, but the tracked quantity is\nthe product, which is what pairs with `|β_h − α| ≤ q_h^{−(2+δ)}` — see the ⚠ in the header for\nwhy the single-`G` form cannot. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mul_pow_sub_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mul_pow_sub_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L224-L230","doc":"The step inequality, per coordinate: peeling `X_j` spends one `γ_j` exactly when the\ncoefficient index has not already outrun the monomial in that coordinate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_coeff_translate_add_le","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L207-L218","doc":"**The tail of the Taylor expansion, bounded.**  Every coefficient of `P` at `α + γ` is at most\n`(#terms)·(max coefficient at `α`)·2^{max degree}·G^{…}` — stated as a single sum bound so that the\nindex hypothesis at `α`, which restricts *which* `n` survive, can be applied to it directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_translateMatrix_le_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_translateMatrix_le_pow","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L199-L205","doc":"**The real instance.**  `|binom(n,i)·γ^{n−i}| ≤ 2^{|n|}·G^{|n|−|i|}` for real `γ` bounded by\n`G ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.submultSeminorm_abs_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.submultSeminorm_abs_real","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L195-L197","doc":"`|·|` on `ℝ` is a submultiplicative seminorm. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.seminorm_translateMatrix_le_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.seminorm_translateMatrix_le_pow","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L100-L193","doc":"**The translate matrix is small when the translation is.**  `f(binom(n,i)·γ^{n−i}) ≤\n2^{|n|}·G^{|n|−|i|}` for `f ∘ γ ≤ G ≤ 1` — the same peeling as `seminorm_translateMatrix_le`, but\ntracking the power of `γ` that the entry actually carries instead of discarding it.\n\nThat difference is the whole of step 2: `γ = β − α` is tiny, and a bound of the form `(2G)^{|n|}`\nwould be true and useless. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.mul_pow_sub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.mul_pow_sub_le","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L84-L98","doc":"The step inequality behind `seminorm_translateMatrix_le_pow`.  `G ≤ 1` is exactly what is\nneeded once the truncated exponent has collapsed — and it is the *only* hypothesis: below the\ncollapse the two sides are equal, so no sign condition on `G` is required.  The linter caught\nthat `0 ≤ G` was never used, and the stronger statement is kept rather than the tidier one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.coeff_translate_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.coeff_translate_add","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L75-L82","doc":"**Taylor's theorem, in the only form Roth's theorem needs.**  The coefficients at `α + γ` are\na `translateMatrix γ`-combination of the coefficients at `α`; an index hypothesis at `α` deletes\nevery low-weight term of the sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.translate_translate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.translate_translate","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothTaylorBound.lean#L63-L73","doc":"**Translating twice is translating by the sum.**  `P(x + α + γ) = (P(x + α))(x + γ)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}